      "reasoning": "All three earlier answers are confirmed by the current evidence. For q-66724, f(x)=2x+4 is strictly increasing, so it is invertible on each listed interval; the source's additional comma does not change the selected answer. For q-78131, the vertical asymptote prevents continuity at -2, while the graph is continuous at 0 and 2; a corner at 0 does not prevent continuity. For q-104051, the filled point gives f(5)=2, while the left and right limits are 2 and 4. Thus f is defined but discontinuous at 5, and the two-sided limit does not exist. Each answer agrees with its own captured worked solution.",
